{"seq":14,"t":"2026-07-26T07:08:00.648Z","type":"tool_result","tool":"pilotage_get_guide","args":{"language":"buildingflow/1","id":"examples"},"result":{"isError":false,"structuredContent":{"guide":{"id":"examples","title":"Worked examples","level":"examples","topics":["read-then-act","input","automation"],"version":"1","body":"# Worked examples\n\n## 1. Read-then-act\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"comfort check\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"id\": \"occ\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"sensor.occupancy\", \"action\": \"read\" },\n    { \"id\": \"gate\", \"do\": \"branch\",\n      \"when\": { \"gt\": [\"$.steps.occ.output.count\", 0] },\n      \"then\": [\n        { \"id\": \"warm\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"hvac.zone1\",\n          \"action\": \"set_target\", \"with\": { \"celsius\": 22 } }\n      ],\n      \"else\": [\n        { \"id\": \"eco\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"hvac.zone1\", \"action\": \"eco_mode\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"output\": { \"path_taken\": \"$.steps.gate.output.took\" }\n}\n```\n\n## 2. Parameterized flow with input\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"set floor2 brightness\",\n  \"input\": { \"fields\": [ { \"name\": \"level\", \"type\": \"number\", \"required\": true } ] },\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"id\": \"east\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"light.floor2_east\",\n      \"action\": \"set_brightness\", \"with\": { \"percent\": \"$.input.level\" } },\n    { \"id\": \"west\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"light.floor2_west\",\n      \"action\": \"set_brightness\", \"with\": { \"percent\": \"$.input.level\" } }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## 3. A deployable automation (needs a trigger; run with mode \"deploy\")\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"dock door alert\",\n  \"trigger\": { \"event\": \"sensor.door_dock.opened\" },\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"id\": \"check\", \"do\": \"branch\",\n      \"when\": { \"gt\": [\"$.world.time\", \"21:00\"] },\n      \"then\": [\n        { \"id\": \"alert\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"notify.facilities\",\n          \"action\": \"send\", \"with\": { \"message\": \"Dock door opened after hours\" } }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nComparison note: `gt`/`lt` compare **two numbers** numerically or **two\nstrings** lexicographically. String comparison on `$.world.time` works\nbecause \"HH:MM\" is zero-padded, so `{\"gt\": [\"$.world.time\", \"21:00\"]}` is\ntrue after 21:00. Comparing a string to a number is a `type_error` at\nvalidation time.\n","language":"buildingflow/1","format":"text/markdown","size_bytes":1836}},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"guide"}]}}
{"seq":15,"t":"2026-07-26T07:08:01.569Z","type":"model_response","finish_reason":"tool_calls","usage":{"prompt_tokens":2540,"completion_tokens":29,"total_tokens":2569,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1664,"audio_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"accepted_prediction_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":0}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nGMioRGtQndFL5fLIYO24c5C","type":"function","function":{"name":"pilotage_get_guide","arguments":"{\"language\":\"buildingflow/1\",\"id\":\"quickstart\"}"}}],"refusal":null,"annotations":[]}}
{"seq":16,"t":"2026-07-26T07:08:01.613Z","type":"tool_result","tool":"pilotage_get_guide","args":{"language":"buildingflow/1","id":"quickstart"},"result":{"isError":false,"structuredContent":{"guide":{"id":"quickstart","title":"Your first flow","level":"core","topics":["shape","steps","expressions","scope-rules","the-loop"],"version":"1","body":"# Your first flow\n\nA **flow** is a JSON document in `buildingflow/1`. The smallest useful flow\nhas one step:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"lobby on\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"id\": \"on\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"light.lobby\", \"action\": \"turn_on\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## The document shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"optional label\",\n  \"input\": { \"fields\": [ { \"name\": \"level\", \"type\": \"number\", \"required\": true } ] },\n  \"trigger\": { \"schedule\": \"22:00\" },\n  \"steps\": [ \"…one or more steps…\" ],\n  \"output\": { \"key\": \"$.steps.someStep.output.someField\" }\n}\n```\n\n- `input` declares the parameters a caller may pass; reference them as\n  `$.input.<name>`.\n- `trigger` is only needed when the flow is **deployed** as an automation:\n  either `{\"event\": \"<device-id>.<event>\"}` or `{\"schedule\": \"HH:MM\"}`.\n- `output` maps result keys to expressions.\n\n## Step kinds (all four)\n\n```json\n{ \"id\": \"a\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"light.lobby\", \"action\": \"set_brightness\",\n  \"with\": { \"percent\": 40 } }\n\n{ \"id\": \"b\", \"do\": \"branch\",\n  \"when\": { \"gt\": [\"$.world.occupancy\", 0] },\n  \"then\": [ \"…steps…\" ], \"else\": [ \"…steps…\" ] }\n\n{ \"id\": \"c\", \"do\": \"for_each\", \"in\": { \"devices\": \"floor2\" }, \"as\": \"d\",\n  \"steps\": [ { \"id\": \"dim\", \"do\": \"call\", \"device\": \"light.floor2_east\",\n               \"action\": \"turn_off\" } ] }\n\n{ \"id\": \"d\", \"do\": \"set\", \"value\": \"$.world.time\" }\n```\n\nStep ids must be unique across the whole flow and may not contain `#`\nor `/`.\n\n## Expressions\n\nAny string starting with `$.` is a path:\n\n| Path | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `$.input.<field>` | a declared input value |\n| `$.steps.<id>.output.<key>` | an earlier step's result |\n| `$.world.time` | the building clock, \"HH:MM\" |\n| `$.world.occupancy` | people currently in the building |\n| `$.item` | the current item inside a `for_each` |\n\nConditions use operator objects: `{\"gt\": [a, b]}`, `{\"lt\": …}`,\n`{\"eq\": …}`, `{\"and\": […]}`, `{\"or\": […]}`, `{\"not\": e}`.\n\n**Scope rule (important):** a step's result becomes addressable *after* the\nstep, in the **parent scope**: this includes steps inside branch arms and\nloop bodies. Write `$.steps.<armStep>.output`, never\n`$.steps.<branchId>.<armStep>`.\n\n## The loop you should follow\n\n1. `pilotage_catalog`: find real device ids (never guess them).\n2. Draft the flow.\n3. `validate_flow`: fix diagnostics until `valid` is true; read the\n   returned `plan` and its `max_risk_hints`.\n4. `run_flow`: with `mode`, your `expected_catalog_version`, and\n   `trace_level: \"full\"`.\n5. Check the trace, especially `decisions`, against what you intended.\n\nSee the reference guide (topic `closed-sets`) for every closed vocabulary,\nand the examples guide for complete flows.\n","language":"buildingflow/1","format":"text/markdown","size_bytes":2653}},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"guide"}]}}
